WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:17.689
Cambodia is far from an ordinary country.

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:22.050
It went through such a bad period that this
place became one of the poorest countries

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.730
with the bleakest prospects in Southeast Asia.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:32.689
You see, sandwiched between two more populous
and emerging economic powers, Vietnam and

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:37.840
Thailand, this small country of fewer than
16 million inhabitants has one of the most

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.960
horrendous, cruel and ruthless histories of
the entire continent and, perhaps, the entire

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:50.680
planet.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.839
In 1975 the Cambodian Communist Party took
control of the country.

00:00:53.839 --> 00:00:59.370
For the next four years, until its downfall
in 1979, the Khmer Rouge – as the party

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:07.060
members were known – perpetrated one of
the worst genocides humanity has ever known.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:12.270
During the existence of the Democratic Kampuchea,
the name of the state ruled by the Khmer Rouge,

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.540
between one and a half million and three million
people lost their lives due to their policies.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:20.160
That’s a quarter of the population of the
entire country.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.830
Wiped out in just four years!

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:29.300
The execution of political dissidents and
racial and religious minorities made up most

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.640
of this chilling figure.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:35.350
Because nobody was safe there.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.630
Muslims, Christians, Buddhists, people of
one ethnic group or another, whomever the

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:45.100
government considered as an enemy of the revolution
was targeted by this “purge”.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:49.550
Yes, the Khmer Rouge was crazy.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:54.210
And of course, all this crippled Cambodia's
development prospects for many years because...

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.240
How can you recover from something so horrendous?

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.200
As you can imagine, it was no easy task.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.790
And yes, that’s exactly what we’re going
to talk about today in this video, about how

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:08.119
Cambodia has changed since the fall of communism,
both in the economic and political fields,

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:13.000
And about what we can expect from this small
Asian country in the future, which is located

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.060
in one of the areas of the world that has
the most potential.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:21.090
Listen up.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:27.310
(A 100% DEPENDENT ECONOMY)

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:34.510
Cambodia has experienced impressive, exponential
economic growth in recent years.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:39.859
Between 1997 and 2017, its GDP has grown every
year at an average of 7.7%.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:50.909
Its GDP per capita has multiplied by more
than three.

00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:52.670
These are excellent numbers, but...

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.620
What exactly has such development translated
into?

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:00.110
Well, for example, this huge economic growth
has meant that the population living below

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:05.799
the poverty line has decreased from approximately
50 to just over 13%.

00:03:05.799 --> 00:03:10.279
And of course, with this data you may think...

00:03:10.279 --> 00:03:11.279
Wow!

00:03:11.279 --> 00:03:13.439
Things seem to be going very well in Cambodia…

00:03:13.439 --> 00:03:14.439
Right?

00:03:14.439 --> 00:03:24.190
Well, yes… and no.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:29.290
The truth is that right now the country is
experiencing – what you could call– a

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.299
great uncertainty.

00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:34.810
It sits between China and the western actors
– the United States and the European Union.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:39.470
But, let's look at this step by step.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:46.579
We’ve already seen the Cambodian economy’s
enormous growth in the last two decades, so

00:03:46.579 --> 00:03:48.310
that raises the question,

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.599
What exactly does Cambodia offer?

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:54.739
What is their economic model based on?

00:03:54.739 --> 00:04:02.639
Well, the answer here is simple: the textile
industry and tourism.

00:04:02.639 --> 00:04:07.319
The powerful Cambodian textile industry accounts
for approximately 80% of the country's exports

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:10.019
and employs more than 700,000 people.

00:04:10.019 --> 00:04:14.680
This industry is by far the country’s driving
force and the main source of income for many

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.299
Cambodian families.

00:04:16.299 --> 00:04:21.870
By the way, Cambodia has a feature that is
seriously harming its development, and it

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:26.400
could also be a huge problem for its future.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.270
Cambodia is still a mostly rural country.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:34.570
Less than 25% of the population lives in cities,
which places it as one of the least urbanized

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:35.570
countries on the planet.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:41.100
To give you an idea of ​​what this figure
means, its neighbor Laos is nearing 40%.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:45.690
Under these conditions, access and provision
of educational services are very expensive

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.040
and difficult to manage.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.950
Most rural schools don’t have books or internet
connection, and people continue to look to

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:54.000
the countryside as a way of life.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.470
This explains why approximately 20% of the
adult population is illiterate.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:02.130
But, let’s not get off topic.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:06.750
The fact is that a large part of Cambodia’s
economic takeoff was due to another character,

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:12.170
a protagonist who arrived with a huge wad
of bills and stacks of bricks under his arm.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:26.130
Do you want to know who’s hiding behind
this sudden deluge

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.130
of investment?

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:31.400
China, China has spent years investing hundreds
of millions of dollars in infrastructure and

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.250
in the construction sector, in real estate
development.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:39.730
In Cambodia, it’s currently very common
to see landscapes full of cranes, and imposing

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.750
buildings and skyscrapers under construction.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:48.740
In the last two years alone, about 6,000 construction
projects valued at more than 11 billion dollars

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:49.740
have been approved.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:56.190
And yes, most of the buyers in this promising
new real estate market come from China.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:06:01.410
Typically between 50 and 80% of the properties
of the most luxurious real estate developments

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:05.560
in the capital, Phnom Penh, are acquired by
Chinese.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:09.500
But, just a second, what has triggered such
fervor?

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.140
Are the Chinese crazy about Cambodia?

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:17.590
Well... maybe, but there’s another compelling
reason:

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:21.720
The poor supervision that Cambodia implements
on the source of money invested as well as

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:27.130
its lax regulations has led many Chinese millionaires
to use Cambodia as a refuge for their money.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.390
You know, in case things go pear-shaped in
China.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:34.870
But of course, there’s two sides to every
coin, and in this story, it’s no different.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:41.630
So far, we’ve seen the attractive face,
but what about the other one?

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:50.140
(HUN SEN, CHINA AND THE DEATH OF DEMOCRACY)

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:54.270
We already told you what’s happening in
the Cambodian economy, but we cannot forget

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:58.740
Hun Sen, the country’s prime minister and
major player in Cambodian news.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:04.030
You see, Hun Sen was one of the main opponents
of the Khmer Rouge’s Maoist regime and reached

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:08.840
power in 1979 with the Vietnamese invasion
that put an end to the Democratic Kampuchea

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:12.120
and the horrors of the Khmer, led by Pol Pot.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:17.920
Since then, Hun Sen has ruled the country,
becoming second on the list of longest ruling

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:22.630
leaders, second only to the Equatorial Guinean
leader, Teodoro Obiang.

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:25.030
And, what can I say?...

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:34.390
At first glance, the fact that a ruler has
been in power for so long doesn’t look good,

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.620
right?

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:41.620
The fact is that in 1993 Hun Sen approved
a new Constitution that, at least on paper,

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:46.050
would democratize the country by turning it
into a constitutional monarchy with a multi-party

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:49.340
system that could allow for a democratically
elected Prime Minister.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:54.210
However, 26 years have passed and there’s
still no trace of democracy.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:58.330
The Constitution exists, but there’s no
opposition because the regime itself doesn’t

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.330
allow it.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.980
And in recent years things have got worse.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:09.010
In the local elections of June 2017, the opposition
party National Rescue of Cambodia achieved

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:11.040
significant popular support.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.700
However, their joy didn’t last long.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:16.650
The Supreme Court, controlled by the Prime
Minister, ordered the dissolution of the opposition

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:20.700
party and the imprisonment of its leader,
Kem Sokha, in November.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.700
The reason?

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:22.700
As is often the case…

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:24.510
The opposition was accused of planning an
uprising.

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:29.170
After the illegalization of the opposition
and the imprisonment of Sokha, which led to

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:33.860
other opposition leaders going into exile,
the Hun Sen regime demonstrated that the political

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:41.130
freedoms promulgated by the 1993 Constitution
were, when it came down to it, merely cosmetic.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:46.370
But such a disregard for democracy and political
freedoms would have consequences.

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:49.970
US House Passes Bill to Sanction Cambodia’s
Top Officials.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:51.500
Voice of America

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:54.300
EU begins process to hit Cambodia with trade
sanctions.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.300
Reuters

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:59.710
And it’s precisely this that can hurt Cambodia
the most: the European Union’s trade sanctions.

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:04.760
Although in reality, it’s not about sanctions,
but about Cambodia’s withdrawal from the

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:09.260
European “All but Arms” program, a program
that benefits the poorest countries by giving

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:13.580
them access to the European market through
tariff exemptions, which has greatly helped

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:18.520
the Cambodian textile industry to develop.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:22.310
But of course, in order to profit from these
commercial advantages, certain conditions

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:26.990
have to be met, and one of them is securing
human rights and political and democratic

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:29.270
freedoms.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:33.420
And it’s precisely because of Hun Sen's
violation of these principles that the EU

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:37.150
is immersed in the process of expelling Cambodia
from this initiative.

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:41.860
THis expulsion may jeopardize a good part
of Cambodia’s textile production, whose

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:46.040
Exports to the European Union account for
about 6 billion dollars, which, in turn equates

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:50.130
to 40% of the country's total exports.

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:55.700
And of course, in the face of such a threat,
the logical thing is for Hun Sen to take a

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:58.190
step back, don't you think?

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:00.680
Well... no, nothing could be further from
the truth.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:05.130
Hun Sen not only reaffirms his position, but
blames the European Union for meddling in

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.130
internal affairs.

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:07.420
But... just a second.

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:11.800
Because if Hun Sen really doesn’t care about
the sanctions and this check on the Cambodian

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:17.170
economy, is the Prime Minister condemning
the country to disaster?

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:25.830
Well... perhaps, but the truth is somewhat
more complicated.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:30.690
What Hun Sen really has in mind is decreasing
their dependence on the West by turning to

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:31.690
China.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:36.430
Moreover, relations with Beijing are so good
that the support is mutual.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:41.930
See, while China floods the Cambodian regime
with aid and investments, Cambodia supports

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:47.140
China in the ASEAN resolutions, which condemn
Beijing's military and territorial expansion

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.650
in the South China Sea.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:50.820
And just a second because that’s not all.

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:51.820
Listen up.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:55.060
China reportedly signs secret deal to station
troops in Cambodia.

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:56.060
The Guardian

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:57.060
Yes, you heard that right.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:58.060
There are significant indications that China
could end up opening a military base in Cambodia.

00:10:58.060 --> 00:10:59.060
A new Chinese military base abroad.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.060
We’ll see how this ends up.

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:01.060
With all this, one thing is very clear...

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.620
Hun Sen has become a Beijing man, and is turning
his back on the West, he’s the latest player

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:04.620
to do so.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:05.620
But now it's your turn…

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:09.790
What do you think about China wielding its
power in Southeast Asia by flashing its checkbook

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:12.330
even at the cost of harming political freedoms?

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:16.710
Should Hun Sen retract and remain more neutral
towards the West and China?

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.360
Leave your answer in the comments.

